# Admin Web (Vite) environment configuration
# Copy to `.env` when you need to override the default.

# Backend origin (scheme + host + port), WITHOUT the `/api` prefix.
# API requests already append `/api/...` (e.g. `/api/auth/login`).
# Do not set this to `http://localhost:8080/api`; a trailing `/api` is
# stripped automatically, but the origin form is clearer.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Leave VITE_API_BASE_URL empty to use the Vite dev proxy (`/api` -> :8080)
# configured in vite.config.ts.

# CORS: the backend must allow this dev origin. Default backend allow-list is
# http://localhost:5173 (Admin Web) and http://localhost:8081 (Expo Web).
# If you serve the web app from another origin, add it to the backend's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS environment variable.
